combination, for the detection of (a) BCC and (b) cSCC, in adults. We separated studies according to whether the        
diagnosis was recorded face‐to‐face (in person) or based on remote (image‐based) assessment.", "background": "Early     
accurate detection of all skin cancer types is important to guide appropriate management, to reduce morbidity and to    
improve survival. Basal cell carcinoma (BCC) is almost always a localised skin cancer with potential to infiltrate and  
damage surrounding tissue, whereas a minority of cutaneous squamous cell carcinomas (cSCCs) and invasive melanomas are  
higher‐risk skin cancers with the potential to metastasise and cause death. Dermoscopy has become an important tool to  
